  "the population is E541's ambiguous rows only, and E541 decides by evidence the census row happens to carry; if that evidence is wrong this study measures the wrong surviving set and cannot tell",
  "the function field can only separate survivors when E541's function arm was refused; whenever that arm applies, every survivor already matches the census function, so a zero function count is a consequence of the arm's order rather than a measurement",
  "the context is the candidate's own AST ancestry at the face's cutoff; a file edited since the upstream face was published shifts the nodes and the row would be published with an unresolved context rather than silently re-located",
  "tier is a property of the row, not of the node, so it can never separate a row's own survivors -- the face publishes that invariance instead of counting it as a difference",
  "distance is candidate line minus published line, so two survivors inside one multi-line statement can differ in distance while agreeing on statement and loop",
  "statement_kind and statement_line are the AST's own reading; a rewrite that changes only formatting moves both and is indistinguishable here from a change of meaning",
  "the class names what separates the survivors, not which survivor the census meant -- a row whose survivors sit in different functions can still have an obvious intended node"
